cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. This is an open research prototype; its benchmark results are synthetic and are not empirical validation of the Ziran / Xeno framework."
type: software
title: "Ziran / Xeno Operational World Simulator: Operational-Shape Dynamics, Observability Generation, and Description-Space Reorganization"
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Fujie"
    given-names: "Naoto"
repository-code: "https://github.com/n-fujie/ziran-xeno-simulator"
url: "https://github.com/n-fujie/ziran-xeno-simulator"
# No DOI has been assigned. If a DOI is issued later, add it here as `doi:` and under `identifiers`.
abstract: >-
  An experimental framework for studying how operational differences ignite under configuration-dependent
  conditions, alter downstream reachability, penetrate across coupled configurations, and reorganize observation
  and description systems. The release supports explicit analysis of configuration reorganization, description-space
  transformation, and partially revisable meta-configuration, with implementation conformance, theory-discriminating
  and meta-boundedness benchmark suites whose results are synthetic.
keywords:
  - simulation
  - observability
  - reachability
  - description space
  - meta-configuration
  - research prototype
